Breaks: A watcher that looks before the chat has claimed its name is told how far the log goes and handed nothing, so it records itself as having announced everything already waiting. The chat then opens and sits idle next to post nobody ever mentions — the one path that reaches an idle chat, silent in exactly the case where somebody was sent work before they opened the chat.
Must fail: go test ./internal/cli -run '^TestWatchStartedBeforeTheChatAnnouncesWhatWasAlreadyThere$' -count=1

